1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:08,742
Meet Cowork Adoption Intelligence: a testing, data-free Power BI template that turns approved Cowork exports into a clear adoption story.

2
00:00:08,743 --> 00:00:17,621
It connects reach, return, organizational patterns, workflow maturity, potential champions, work mix, and modeled assisted time.

3
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:21,718
Start Here routes program owners to the right question.

4
00:00:21,719 --> 00:00:23,490
Is adoption building momentum?

5
00:00:23,491 --> 00:00:25,061
Where is it strongest?

6
00:00:25,062 --> 00:00:26,656
How mature is usage?

7
00:00:26,657 --> 00:00:32,609
Begin with the decision, then open the page that carries the right evidence and interpretation boundary.

8
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:36,504
Executive Summary reads the latest active week.

9
00:00:36,505 --> 00:00:38,537
Weekly active users show reach.

10
00:00:38,538 --> 00:00:41,728
Prompts, return rate, and active days show habit.

11
00:00:41,729 --> 00:00:51,251
The momentum score balances return, consistency, intensity, and advanced delegation, so share it with the week, filters, weights, and caps.

12
00:00:52,173 --> 00:00:56,292
Weekly Adoption and Usage shows the latest twelve active weeks.

13
00:00:56,293 --> 00:01:02,670
Switch among reach, momentum, prompts, active days, and return rate without clearing filters.

14
00:01:02,671 --> 00:01:10,265
Use the heatmap to find concentration, then check rollout timing, holidays, and export coverage before calling a trend.

15
00:01:11,173 --> 00:01:17,434
Adoption by Attributes compares observed task volume and delegation patterns by department or country.

16
00:01:17,435 --> 00:01:20,730
These views depend on optional organization enrichment.

17
00:01:20,731 --> 00:01:25,099
Always check population size and mapping coverage before comparing groups.

18
00:01:26,013 --> 00:01:34,048
User Maturity combines the delegation ladder, multi-skill task share, task duration, and rolling twelve-week usage tiers.

19
00:01:34,049 --> 00:01:39,534
Scheduled-task totals are lifetime-scoped, while the other rungs follow the selected period.

20
00:01:39,535 --> 00:01:43,129
Pair every maturity signal with role and work context.

21
00:01:44,047 --> 00:01:49,189
Cowork Champions identifies potential enablement partners, not top performers.

22
00:01:49,190 --> 00:01:53,473
Eligibility requires three observed threads across two active weeks.

23
00:01:53,474 --> 00:02:01,044
The evidence score balances activity, consistency, and delegation maturity, then applies the selected percentile tier.

24
00:02:01,959 --> 00:02:08,935
Activity and Assisted Hours connects observed Cowork records to low, mid, or high time-saved assumptions.

25
00:02:08,936 --> 00:02:14,016
Category results are allocated estimates, not per-skill metering or a time study.

26
00:02:14,017 --> 00:02:18,420
Present a range and label every result as modeled assisted time.

27
00:02:19,325 --> 00:02:25,729
What They Use It For groups observed skills into work patterns and preserves action and user detail behind bookmarks.

28
00:02:25,730 --> 00:02:30,167
Action value tiers are declared category references, not user scores.

29
00:02:30,168 --> 00:02:35,132
Review unmapped skills and validate dominant categories before recommending a workflow.

30
00:02:36,037 --> 00:02:41,548
Momentum Score Guide explains the live adoption signal before exposing optional controls.

31
00:02:41,549 --> 00:02:49,987
The default weights are thirty-five percent return, twenty-five percent consistency, twenty-five percent intensity, and fifteen percent maturity.

32
00:02:49,988 --> 00:02:54,617
If the weights do not total one hundred percent, the score becomes blank.

33
00:02:55,537 --> 00:03:04,763
The Adoption Metric Guide defines all ten report pages, with evidence status, thresholds, dependencies, and interpretation boundaries.

34
00:03:04,764 --> 00:03:10,427
Copy the definition, reporting period, filters, and status into decision records.

35
00:03:10,428 --> 00:03:15,367
This is decision support, not billing, compliance, or personnel evidence.

36
00:03:16,281 --> 00:03:28,888
That is Cowork Adoption Intelligence: one testing template for reach, return, organizational patterns, workflow maturity, champions, work mix, and transparent assisted-time scenarios.

37
00:03:28,889 --> 00:03:34,957
Start with the fabricated sample, review the definitions, then connect approved exports when ready.
